1
00:00:02,790 --> 00:00:05,130
- Okay, let's start with the basics.
- Yes!

2
00:00:05,130 --> 00:00:06,800
Let's read "Uirouri."

3
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:08,430
"Uirouri"?

4
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:11,430
I am known as the shopkeeper.

5
00:00:11,430 --> 00:00:13,930
I... I am known as the shopkeeper...

6
00:00:13,930 --> 00:00:15,060
Try projecting from your diaphragm.

7
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:16,060
Okay.

8
00:00:17,060 --> 00:00:19,940
I am known as the shopkeeper.

9
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:21,940
Among those present here...

10
00:00:21,940 --> 00:00:24,190
Some of you may already know me...

11
00:00:24,190 --> 00:00:25,230
Relax a bit.

12
00:00:25,230 --> 00:00:26,400
Okay.

13
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,030
Take a deep breath.

14
00:00:30,450 --> 00:00:32,490
I...

15
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:35,790
(This is so embarrassing...)

16
00:00:35,790 --> 00:00:38,620
Repeat after me.

17
00:00:38,620 --> 00:00:39,790
Okay.

18
00:00:40,830 --> 00:00:43,000
If I were a woman,

19
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,750
If I were a woman,

20
00:00:46,710 --> 00:00:48,760
I would love you with all my heart,

21
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:51,970
I would love you with all my heart,

22
00:00:51,970 --> 00:00:54,720
and adore you beyond reason.

23
00:00:54,720 --> 00:00:57,770
and adore you beyond reason.

24
00:00:57,770 --> 00:00:59,600
Oh!

25
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:01,230
Look at how much you've improved!

26
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:03,810
Thank you, Haru senpai.

27
00:01:03,810 --> 00:01:04,860
In Shakespeare's time,

28
00:01:04,860 --> 00:01:06,610
there were no microphones.

29
00:01:07,320 --> 00:01:09,440
You had to project from the stage

30
00:01:09,780 --> 00:01:11,860
- to make your voice fill the entire theater.
- Yes.

31
00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:13,410
You must deliver your voice

32
00:01:14,370 --> 00:01:15,240
to every single member

33
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:17,700
- of the audience.
- Yes.

34
00:01:18,830 --> 00:01:19,830
Alright!

35
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:22,040
Let's work on your core!

36
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:22,830
Huh?!

37
00:01:22,830 --> 00:01:24,250
- Come on, take it off. Core workout!
- Huh? What?

38
00:01:24,250 --> 00:01:26,210
- Up we go!
- Huh?

39
00:01:26,210 --> 00:01:27,420
Do I... really need strength training?

40
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:29,090
Of course you do.

41
00:01:29,090 --> 00:01:30,760
It's to project a powerful voice!

42
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:32,630
Alright, let's begin!

43
00:01:33,180 --> 00:01:34,760
Okay, one!

44
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:35,720
One...

45
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:37,640
Okay, two!

46
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:39,020
Two...

47
00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:41,770
Too slow! Put some back into it!

48
00:01:42,940 --> 00:01:44,650
Ready, and one!

49
00:01:44,650 --> 00:01:45,690
Back to one again...

50
00:01:45,690 --> 00:01:48,020
Two!

51
00:01:48,690 --> 00:01:50,940
*pant* *pant*

52
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:52,320
Is being an actor

53
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:54,280
always this tough?

54
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:55,120
No.

55
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:57,080
This is just a piece of cake.

56
00:01:57,080 --> 00:01:58,700
Oh, my god...

57
00:01:58,700 --> 00:02:00,910
An actor must

58
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:03,830
use nothing but their body

59
00:02:03,830 --> 00:02:06,750
to convey their performance to the audience.

60
00:02:06,750 --> 00:02:10,050
You've got potential.

61
00:02:10,050 --> 00:02:11,590
Let's do our best together.

62
00:02:11,590 --> 00:02:14,050
Okay... *pant*

63
00:02:17,470 --> 00:02:19,140
Oh, shoot!

64
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:21,180
I forgot I have work today.

65
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:22,480
Huh?! Don't you need to go?

66
00:02:22,480 --> 00:02:23,390
It's fine, don't worry about it.

67
00:02:23,390 --> 00:02:24,560
This is more important.

68
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:25,100
No, no, no.

69
00:02:25,100 --> 00:02:26,600
Please don't worry about me. You should go.

70
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:28,020
It's really fine.

71
00:02:28,020 --> 00:02:29,110
Huh?

72
00:02:29,110 --> 00:02:30,480
What nonsense are you talking?

73
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:32,150
Besides,

74
00:02:32,150 --> 00:02:33,440
if you don't pass the audition,

75
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:34,900
you won't be able to perform on stage.

76
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:37,320
But I just joined the club.

77
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:39,080
There's no way
I can audition already.

78
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:40,370
For our next production,

79
00:02:40,370 --> 00:02:42,700
I want you to audition,
so we have to practice!

80
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:43,870
Whaaat?!

81
00:02:46,620 --> 00:02:47,790
Oh, no.

82
00:02:47,790 --> 00:02:49,170
- The last train!
- Yes!

83
00:02:49,170 --> 00:02:50,340
The last train is leaving!

84
00:02:50,340 --> 00:02:51,630
Hurry, hurry!

85
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:53,590
Ah.

86
00:02:54,170 --> 00:02:56,260
The last train has already left...

87
00:02:56,260 --> 00:02:58,090
What should I do...
